   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Sentiment analysis with hotel reviews\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Why is it important to clean data before analyzing it?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Some columns might have missing or incorrect data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Some columns do seem incorrect, but messy data can also throw off your counts. Both are reasons.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Messy data can lead to false conclusions about the dataset</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Messy data can throw off your results, but some columns are also useless or incorrect. Both are reasons.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Some columns are useless or incorrect, and messy data, like tags in a different order, can throw off your counts.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is one example of a strategy for cleaning data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>removing columns/rows that aren't useful for answering a specific question</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. You drop columns you don't need, and ask whether data, like the tags, is useful for your goal.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>getting rid of verified values that don't fit your hypothesis</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You decide what to drop by whether it is useful for your goal, not by whether it fits your guess.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>moving the outliers to a separate table and running the calculations for that table to see if they match</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The cleaning steps here do not move outliers. They add useful columns, change values in others, and drop some columns.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>It can be useful to categorize data using a Tag column.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Once cleaned up, tags like business trip or with a pet give useful information for recommending a hotel.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The Tag column takes work to clean up, but its tags give useful information when recommending a hotel.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the goal of the dataset?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>to see how many negative and positive reviews there are for hotels across the world</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Counting reviews is not the goal. The goal is to add sentiment and columns that help you pick the best hotel.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>to add sentiment and columns that will help you choose the best hotel</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The goal is to add sentiment and columns that will help you choose the best hotel.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>to analyze why people leave specific reviews</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The goal is to add sentiment and columns that help you choose the best hotel, not to study why people review.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What are stop words?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>common English words that do not change the sentiment of a sentence</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is true, but removing stop words also makes sentiment analysis run faster. Both are true.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>words that you can remove to speed up sentiment analysis</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is true, but stop words are also common English words that do not change a sentence's sentiment.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Stop words are common English words that do not change sentiment. Removing them makes the analysis run faster.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-5-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>To test the sentiment analysis, make sure it matches the reviewer's score for the same review.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. You test the sentiment by comparing it to the reviewer's score for the same review.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Comparing the sentiment to the reviewer's score for the same review is how you test it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
